Rotations:-
Added implementations for right and left rotations of a list, including 1-time and 3-times rotations with time and space complexity analysis.

1 time right rotation:--

l=[1,2,3,4,5]
n=len(l)
temp=l[n-1]
for i in range(n-1,0,-1):
    l[i]=l[i-1]
l[0]=temp
print(l) 

Output:[5,1,2,3,4]
T.C = O(n)
S.C = O(1)


1 time left rotation:--

l=[1,2,3,4,5]
n=len(l)
temp=l[0]
for i in range(0,n-1,1):
    l[i]=l[i+1]
l[n-1]=temp
print(l)

Output:[2,3,4,5,1]
T.C = O(n)
S.C = O(1)




3 times right rotation:__

def rev(l,start,end):
    while start<end:
        temp=l[start]
        l[start]=l[end]
        l[end]=temp
        start=start+1
        end=end-1
l=[1,2,3,4,5,6,7]
n=len(l)
k=3
k=k%n
rev(l,n-k,n-1)
rev(l,0,n-k-1)
rev(l,0,n-1)
print(l)
    
Output:- [5, 6, 7, 1, 2, 3, 4]
T.C = O(n)
S.C = O(1)



3 times left rotation:-

def rev(l,start,end):
    while start<end:
        temp=l[start]
        l[start]=l[end]
        l[end]=temp
        start=start+1
        end=end-1
l=[1,2,3,4,5,6,7]
n=len(l)
k=3
k=k%n
rev(l,0,k-1)
rev(l,k,n-1)
rev(l,0,n-1)
print(l)
    
Output:-- [4,5,6,7,1,2,3]
T.C = O(n)
S.C = O(1)

